WEBVTT

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.100
She's in a state of clinical death.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.700
Hi...ra...

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.960
I'm sorry for the disturbance this may have caused.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.180
I am the Second Ship Captain of the National Defense Organization, Circus.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:13.970
Hirato.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.400
I'll come back at a later time to make an apology.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.440
We'll be going now.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:29.780
Circus...

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:19.300
<i>Yukki.</i>

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.800
Tears of the Beast Handler
Score 10

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.270
We need to register your voice,
so say something, anything you want.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.560
He-Hello.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.020
I'm coming in.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.150
<i>Making people say “I'm home,” must be Yogi's taste.</i>

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.530
Voice registration has been completed.
<i>Making people say “I'm home,” must be Yogi's taste.</i>

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.490
Welcome to the First Ship of Circus.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:50.290
First of all, you two will make sure this room is spotless.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:55.170
Make sure to finish by my return.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:59.670
I'm sorry if you were expecting to be treated as guests.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.840
The Second Ship is full of idiots,
so maybe this job's too hard for you.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.180
Gareki?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.100
I'll finish it instantly.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.100
It'll be fun to see if you can finish it by the time I come back.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.070
<i>Kii-chan is putting in a lot of effort into this.</i>

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.530
<i>It would be easier if we just left them alone.</i>

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.240
<i>We know pretty much everything about Nai.</i>

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.290
<i>As for him... He doesn't have a family register, huh?</i>

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.290
<i>Blood relatives are unknown.</i>

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.370
<i>And he was abandoned at Karasuna, too?</i>

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.210
<i>He was on a human trafficking ship that ran aground?</i>

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.840
<i>Isn't this the incident Tsukitachi-san and Hirato-san took care of?</i>

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.720
Damn it.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.260
There is no end.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.310
What's wrong?

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.940
Because I've been working outside for a while, I got furballs.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.150
Huh? Aren't you a high performance rabbit?

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:07.200
Can't you program yourself not to get furballs?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.660
I'll brush you.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.080
Thank you, Usa.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.910
It feels nice, Usa.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.670
Did he already forget that the cleaning for this room isn't finished yet?

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.170
What?

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.050
<i>I give up.</i>

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.680
<i>I guess I've lost this match to that girl.</i>

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.680
Okay, everyone come here.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.060
What?!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.650
Hi, Kiichi-chan. We'll be done in a minute.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.530
Why are the rabbits helping you?!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.450
Sorry, did I take too long?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.910
Hey, I'm back.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.080
They found Tsukumo-chan?!

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.790
Aren't you glad?

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.630
Hurrah! Hurrah!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:07.050
Well, Yogi's still fast asleep so you two will have to stay here a little longer.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.100
If you have any questions, I'll answer anything you want to know.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.930
Is Tsubame–How is she?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.100
She's doing just fine.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.020
And she's always worrying about you, Gareki.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.860
There's no need for her to worry about me.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:30.360
Since she is under the protection of Circus, her movements are restricted.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.780
But in return, we'll take care of Tsubame's grandfather.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:34.540
What?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.620
She was also happy by the fact that now she doesn't have to burden...

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.750
the benefactor who's been paying her hospital fees.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:49.260
I see. I'm glad for the old man too.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:51.800
Ga–

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.310
Speaking of which, what's the mechanism behind your weapons?

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.520
Oh, are you interested, kiddo?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.440
Then how about we go and take a look for ourselves tomorrow!

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.230
What?!

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.150
Why are you inviting random people for no reason?

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.320
There's indeed a reason.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:09.570
It's the place where the Circus bracelet, the very source of our powers, originates from!

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.410
We haven't even been able to lock down on our enemies yet.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.320
What if something goes wrong?

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.580
There's no danger since all of us will be with them.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.330
Right, Kiichi?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.910
Of course.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.830
I, Kiichi, am different from gofers of the Second Ship.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.170
Let's eat.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.630
We'll be having a field trip tomorrow.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.340
Did you really just say field trip?

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.090
Just how the hell do you view your job, you idiot!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.550
I'm sorry for bringing you here.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.600
But it'll be the first time we do things together

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.600
I want to see how you two react.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.850
Can you try running away from me without being caught?

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.230
Sure.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:48.820
<i> He was blown away by the rabbit back then, wasn't he?</i>

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.360
Then let's start.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.080
Up until now, the enemy hasn't show his true colors.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.000
If they were to get serious, you'd die in a second.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:10.840
This isn't a place where you can survive by going along or being friendly.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.140
To put it bluntly, Gareki-kun, aren't you just a sacrificial pawn used to maintain

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.850
Nai-kun in a stable condition?

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:22.100
You should stop going along with dirty grown-ups,

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.100
and instead return to where you belong.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.440
Well then, let's have fun tomorrow.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.620
<i>Let's enjoy tomorrow.</i>

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.210
Where are you going?

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:52.300
Ah?

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.810
You wanted to talk to Jiki?

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.770
Did he say something?

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.230
Tsukitachi-san.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:08.730
Yes?

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:12.860
I... don't want Gareki a sacrifice.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:16.200
What? Oh, I see.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.240
Let's try rephrasing what you just said.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.450
Um...

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:23.870
Everyone gets into danger because I'm with them. But...

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:27.790
Nai, you think everyone gets hurt because of you?

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.250
Yes.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:35.050
But it's also because you agreed to stay with Circus that
the Varuga whom we want to catch are drawn to us,

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.380
so you're helping us out a lot.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:42.260
You should take advantage of the situation and use us to help find Karoku.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:46.270
Even if something were to happen, we should all overcome it together.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.980
No one will blame you.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:54.110
Well, I had asked Gareki to come along with me.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.490
That's why he often gets into danger.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:00.370
If we part ways, Gareki can go home...

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.870
Nai, where do you want to go back to?

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:03.910
What?

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.710
I wonder where Gareki wants to go back to.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.210
Both of you are involved with Varuga,

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.630
so it may be hard to fulfill your wishes.

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:15.420
Though,

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:20.800
don't you and Gareki have dreams in your heart?

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.810
Dreams in our hearts?

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:33.570
Choose the best thing you can do now in order to get a step closer to your dream.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:39.530
If you care for others, don't just feel guilty but get to know their dreams.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.410
No! Stop, please stop!

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.870
Sorry, but I’m in a hurry.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:49.160
Just make up some kind of excuse to Akari-sens–

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.370
Go back to sleep!

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.580
Akari-sensei.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:57.050
But! I can't bear the thought of Gareki-kun and Nai-chan having gone to the First Ship.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.220
I'm sure they're being bullied!

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.600
Members of the First Ship have left for that investigation yesterday.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.020
You mean to Vinto?

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:08.140
It appears that Nai and Gareki have gone with them.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.850
I'm sure they'll get along just like you guys did.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:24.490
Vinto is a government wildlife sanctuary that protects rare and unique creatures.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:31.330
However, many animals are being poached and also the bodies of poachers have been found…

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:35.500
There's no use in explaining to them, since they won't understand anyway.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:40.470
Hey, both of you, try not to get in our way.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.890
Ah, you are…

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.860
I'm Azana from the Life Division.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.520
It's been quite a while since Rinoll.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.030
How'd you get hurt?

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:04.570
Well, they were inflicted by animals who tend to show their affection by playing with me...

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:05.620
We don't need any chit-chat.
Well, they were inflicted by animals who tend to show their affection by playing with me...

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.030
We don't need any chit-chat.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:10.290
Let's just get on to the investigation.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.830
To work more effectively, let's split into two groups.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:17.290
Personnel from Life Division, please lead the way.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.590
Do you want to come with me, Gareki?

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:22.050
I'll tell you about that source of our powers.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.930
I'll go.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.010
Me too.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.640
Nai-kun, shall we go?

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.640
Nai-kun, shall we go?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:32.390
Jiki-kun, you forgot your guide.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.730
Jiki-kun, you forgot your guide.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:42.990
<i>I'm fine with ignoring other people, but when it's the opposite it pisses me off.</i>

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:48.120
Ever since the bodies of poachers were discovered,

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:50.370
the number of animals being killed have decreased.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.330
Ouch, ouch, ouch.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:55.750
This one in particular was badly hurt by a poacher.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.330
What happened to that poacher?

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.960
I heard he died.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.590
Who found him?

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.470
Murano-senpai and I did.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.630
I see.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.850
I'm glad the animal survived.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:13.810
Are you okay?

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.020
Were you able to sleep last night?

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.440
I'm fine.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:23.940
Circus bracelets are made using the cells of the creatures here.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:29.320
This is a severe environment with limited sunlight and food.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:35.210
Creatures here have managed to evolve themselves in order to survive the harsh conditions.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:39.420
They focused their evolution in high energy production and regenerative capabilities.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:45.050
We extracted such cells, and through research, we came up with...

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.220
Incura, the omnipotent cell.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:54.560
This is the cell that's embedded into our bracelets and enables our powers to materialize.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.810
Go.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.440
Are those also what you call "materializing"?

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.530
Yes. But it's also a double-edged sword.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:08.280
What?

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:12.280
Manipulating the Incura cell isn't something that simple

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.370
If you release its power completely without any control,

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.330
you'll be overwhelmed by it.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:22.710
Well, members of Circus are selected from people who have the capability to handle such power

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:26.760
and have gone through rigorous training.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.350
Bodies of poachers were found around here.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:35.600
Looking at the situation, I think we can conclude the culprits were Varuga, right?

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.310
So it's really done by Varuga?

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:45.070
According to the report, targets were limited to poachers.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:50.410
Jiki-kun, I heard something coming.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.820
Jiki-kun, I heard something coming.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.500
It's just a moss lizard.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.300
That's not what I heard.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:07.670
What?

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:14.300
Murano-senpai!

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:18.140
Kiri, these people are not poachers!

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.520
It's this creature.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.360
It's wary of humans,

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.900
because it had been attacked by a poacher.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.240
This is bad. Kiri, calm down!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.830
This is bad. Kiri, calm down!

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.370
Kiri...

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:51.760
Stop!

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.640
Kiri has done nothing wrong!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:59.020
I know. That's exactly why what you did was an act of great sin.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:04.020
You're one of us brought together by the same mission,

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.980
but I can't give you special treatment.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.110
Run, Kiri!

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.200
So they've hit the jackpot, huh?

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.740
What do you mean by "jackpot"?

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:19.910
Nothing to worry about.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.500
Kiichi and Jiki are with Nai.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.830
Kiri!

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.390
Oh no!

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:40.970
Yogi!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.020
<i>Gather!</i>

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.020
Kiri!

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:54.530
Nai-chan, are you okay?

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.320
Nai-chan, are you okay?

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.660
Yeah.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.660
What should I have done?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:05.580
If I hadn't given that drug to Kiri that time, he would've been dead.

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:11.260
I was so scared of losing Kiri that I didn't care if the drug would make him lose control.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:16.180
I wanted to have such capabilities

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:19.260
to be able to protect everyone I care for.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:25.560
Tell me how you obtained that drug.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.520
I don't know his name.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:32.110
But he claimed to work for Akari-sensei, so I trusted him.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.940
That's so vague.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.240
Well, I guess that's okay for now.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.910
We'll have plenty of time for the interrogation.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.790
No way! All Senpai wanted was to protect animals...

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:48.880
Jiki-kun...

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:51.800
Yogi...

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.810
I'll end your misery soon.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.980
Your sacrifice will not be in vain.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.900
My sickle will surely reach the evil within you.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:34.000
Kiichi-chan...

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.140
Ah, Yogi...

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.640
Gareki-kun!

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.930
You called my name for the first time, didn't you?

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:48.810
What?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.350
I'm so glad!

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:54.820
You've never called my name so I had thought you really hated me.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.030
What are you talking about?

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:59.240
It's not the first time, right? Well, not that I ever really thought about this consciously...

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.990
No, never!

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:02.370
Yes, I did!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.160
It's just you weren't listening!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.450
At Rinoll, when you were unconscious...

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:13.710
I'm really sorry about what happened at Rinoll.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:18.760
Are you physically okay?

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.550
I'm fine now.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:24.100
Let's go back together to the warmth of the Second Ship!

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.940
I'm home!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.650
Welcome back.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:32.810
Welcome back.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.110
I'm home.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:37.230
Gareki-kun,

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:38.150
what's wrong?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.740
You should be saying "I'm home," right?

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:44.700
I'm home.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.700
Welcome back.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:48.910
Tsukumo-chan!

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:00.630
Jiki-kun? Why are you here?

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:01.630
Jiki-kun? Why are you here?

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:05.720
I have orders to stay with Nai-kun and Gareki-kun for the time being.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.640
I look forward to it.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:15.270
Is he okay?

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:16.150
Huh?

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.360
Oh, yes.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:21.650
That's good. Thank you.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.660
It's such a pain in the neck.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.740
When I see him, I feel like my luck would go down.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.250
Karoku-sama's condition seems to be pretty stable these days.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.960
He'll eventually become just bones and skin anyway.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:35.790
It's such a waste to give him food.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:42.470
I want Gareki to tell me something.

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:43.260
What?

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.140
Where do you want to go back to?

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:46.090
Come again?

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.100
Where? Where?

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:47.850
Where? Where?

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:48.510
Where? Where? Where?

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:49.140
Where? Where? Where?

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:49.760
Where? Where? Where?

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:50.850
Shut up!

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:51.850
I don't have such a place!

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.400
<i>I froze for a moment just now.</i>

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:02.110
<i>I thought he saw right through me.</i>

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:08.120
<i>I know damn well that there's nothing much I can do!</i>

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:14.160
<i>But I wanted to change. I wanted to go out there and prove myself.</i>

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.000
<i>But in the end, what did I achieve?</i>

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.880
<i>Place I want to go back to?</i>

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.380
<i>I don't have such a place, nor would I have the right to go there!</i>

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.180
You should be saying "I'm home," right?

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:30.140
<i>But I want to stay here little longer.</i>

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:35.560
Gareki, I want to stay where everyone is.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:39.110
And, I'll be happy if I can find Karoku safe and sound.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:44.110
So to make that happen, I'll do a lot of things.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.910
Your words don't make any sense.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:53.870
I see... So Yogi has evolved into such a simple form.

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.960
The room's all cleaned up so there's no problem, right?

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.250
It's not fair to use the rabbits!

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:32.710
That reminds me: I have these eclairs that you love so much.

00:23:32.710 --> 00:23:34.130
Hurray! I'll have them!

00:23:34.130 --> 00:23:35.380
Jiki, where are you?

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:38.470
Jiki-kun's not around so I'll eat his share!
